{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -L 'https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:24258910%20AND%20SRC:MED&resultType=core&format=json'\"","aggregated_output":"\r100  5409    0  540{\"version\":\"6.9\",\"hitCount\":1,\"request\":{\"queryString\":\"EXT_ID:24258910 AND SRC:MED\",\"internalQuery\":\"EXT_ID:24258910 AND SRC:MED\",\"resultType\":\"CORE\",\"cursorMark\":\"*\",\"pageSize\":25,\"sort\":\"\",\"synonym\":false},\"resultList\":{\"result\":[{\"id\":\"24258910\",\"source\":\"MED\",\"pmid\":\"24258910\",\"doi\":\"10.1002/eji.201343751\",\"title\":\"The who's who of T-cell differentiation: human memory T-cell subsets.\",\"authorString\":\"Mahnke YD, Brodie TM, Sallusto F, Roederer M, Lugli E.\",\"authorList\":{\"author\":[{\"fullName\":\"Mahnke YD\",\"firstName\":\"Yolanda D\",\"lastName\":\"Mahnke\",\"initials\":\"YD\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-2727-9887\"},\"authorAffiliationDetailsList\":{\"authorAffiliation\":[{\"affiliation\":\"Translational and Correlative Studies Laboratory, Abramson Family Cancer Research Center, Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania, PA, USA.\"}]}},{\"fullName\":\"Brodie TM\",\"firstName\":\"Tess M\",\"lastName\":\"Brodie\",\"initials\":\"TM\"},{\"fullName\":\"Sallusto F\",\"firstName\":\"Federica\",\"lastName\":\"Sallusto\",\"initials\":\"F\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0003-3750-2752\"}},{\"fullName\":\"Roederer M\",\"firstName\":\"Mario\",\"lastName\":\"Roederer\",\"initials\":\"M\"},{\"fullName\":\"Lugli E\",\"firstName\":\"Enrico\",\"lastName\":\"Lugli\",\"initials\":\"E\",\"authorId\":{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-1964-7678\"}}]},\"authorIdList\":{\"authorId\":[{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-1964-7678\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0002-2727-9887\"},{\"type\":\"ORCID\",\"value\":\"0000-0003-3750-2752\"}]},\"dataLinksTagsList\":{\"dataLinkstag\":[\"altmetrics\"]},\"journalInfo\":{\"issue\":\"11\",\"volume\":\"43\",\"journalIssueId\":2096975,\"dateOfPublication\":\"2013 Nov\",\"monthOfPublication\":11,\"yearOfPublication\":2013,\"printPublicationDate\":\"2013-11-01\",\"journal\":{\"title\":\"European journal of immunology\",\"medlineAbbreviation\":\"Eur J Immunol\",\"isoabbreviation\":\"Eur J Immunol\",\"nlmid\":\"1273201\",\"essn\":\"1521-4141\",\"issn\":\"0014-2980\"}},\"pubYear\":\"2013\",\"pageInfo\":\"2797-2809\",\"abstractText\":\"Following antigen encounter and subsequent resolution of the immune response, a single naïve T cell is able to generate multiple subsets of memory T cells with different phenotypic and functional properties and gene expression profiles. Single-cell technologies, first and foremost flow cytometry, have revealed the complex heterogeneity of the memory T-cell compartment and its organization into subsets. However, a consensus has still to be reached, both at the semantic (nomenclature) and phenotypic level, regarding the identification of these subsets. Here, we review recent developments in the characterization of the heterogeneity of the memory T-cell compartment, and propose a unified classification of both human and nonhuman primate T cells on the basis of phenotypic traits and in vivo properties. Given that vaccine studies and adoptive cell transfer immunotherapy protocols are influenced by these recent findings, it is important to use uniform methods for identifying and discussing functionally distinct subsets of T cells.\",\"affiliation\":\"Translational and Correlative Studies Laboratory, Abramson Family Cancer Research Center, Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania, PA, USA.\",\"publicationStatus\":\"ppublish\",\"language\":\"eng\",\"pubModel\":\"Print-Electronic\",\"pubTypeList\":{\"pubType\":[\"Research Support, N.I.H., Intramural\",\"Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't\",\"Review\",\"Journal Article\"]},\"grantsList\":{\"grant\":[{\"agency\":\"Intramural NIH HHS\",\"orderIn\":0}]},\"meshHeadingList\":{\"meshHeading\":[{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"T-Lymphocyte Subsets\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"CY\",\"qualifierName\":\"cytology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"IM\",\"qualifierName\":\"immunology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\"},{\"abbreviation\":\"ME\",\"qualifierName\":\"metabolism\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Humans\"},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Adoptive Transfer\"},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Immunotherapy, Adoptive\"},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Lymphocyte Activation\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"IM\",\"qualifierNam9    0     0  13157      0 --:--:-- --:--:-- --:--:-- 13192\ne\":\"immunology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Cell Differentiation\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"IM\",\"qualifierName\":\"immunology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Immunologic Memory\",\"meshQualifierList\":{\"meshQualifier\":[{\"abbreviation\":\"IM\",\"qualifierName\":\"immunology\",\"majorTopic_YN\":\"Y\"}]}},{\"majorTopic_YN\":\"N\",\"descriptorName\":\"Gene Expression\"}]},\"keywordList\":{\"keyword\":[\"Flow cytometry\",\"Naïve T Cells\",\"Human T-cell Subsets\",\"Memory T-cell Differentiation\"]},\"subsetList\":{\"subset\":[{\"code\":\"IM\",\"name\":\"Index Medicus\"}]},\"fullTextUrlList\":{\"fullTextUrl\":[{\"availability\":\"Subscription required\",\"availabilityCode\":\"S\",\"documentStyle\":\"doi\",\"site\":\"DOI\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1002/eji.201343751\"}]},\"isOpenAccess\":\"N\",\"inEPMC\":\"N\",\"inPMC\":\"N\",\"hasPDF\":\"N\",\"hasBook\":\"N\",\"hasSuppl\":\"N\",\"citedByCount\":666,\"hasData\":\"N\",\"hasReferences\":\"Y\",\"hasTextMinedTerms\":\"Y\",\"hasDbCrossReferences\":\"N\",\"hasLabsL